# laravel-blog-app — E2E Tests

E2E tests for [laravelblogapplication.vercel.app](https://laravelblogapplication.vercel.app/), a Laravel blog app I built and deployed.

## Scope

`Posts`, `Products`, and `Register` are currently work-in-progress placeholder pages on the site itself. Instead of faking flows that don't exist yet, this suite covers:

- Navigation and smoke checks
- Language switching (EN / DE / RU)
- Light/dark theme toggle
- Login form rendering and client-side (HTML5) validation
- Placeholder pages rendering correctly instead of erroring out

`tests/login.spec.ts` has a `test.skip` placeholder for the full authenticated-login flow, to enable once a seeded test account exists.

## Structure

```
laravel-blog-app/
├── pages/              # Page Object Model
│   ├── BasePage.ts
│   ├── HomePage.ts
│   └── LoginPage.ts
├── tests/
│   ├── navigation.spec.ts
│   ├── i18n.spec.ts
│   ├── theme.spec.ts
│   ├── login.spec.ts
│   └── placeholder-pages.spec.ts
└── playwright.config.ts
```

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npx playwright install --with-deps
```

## Run

```bash
npm test              # headless, all browsers
npm run test:headed   # watch it run
npm run test:ui       # interactive UI mode
npm run report        # open last HTML report
```

